  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAuditor of Jones County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n Jones County, Iowa\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n Search\n \n \n \n\n \n\n Departments\n \n \n \n\n 911 Address Coordinator\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor\n Board of Supervisors\n Children Services\n Clerk of Court\n Community Services\n Conservation\n DHS (Human Services)\n Emergency Management\n Environmental Health\n GIS\n JETS\n Land Use\n Landfill\n Public Health\n Recorder\n Secondary Roads\n Senior Dining\n Sheriff\n Treasurer\n Veteran Affairs\n \n \n \n\n Resources\n \n \n \n\n Bid Notices\n Calendar\n Elections \n Employment\n FAQ\n Resource Guide\n Safety Action Plan \n \n \n \n\n About\n \n \n \n\n Agendas & Minutes\n Boards & Commissions\n Communities\n Community Links\n County Ordinances\n Employee Information\n School Districts\n Township Information\n \n \n \n\n Contact\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n \nDepartments\n \n\nAuditor \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nOur goals in serving the citizens of Jones County:\nTo provide accurate and reliable financial records, with full and complete disclosure of the county’s finances.\nTo preserve integrity and fairness in the election process.\nTo provide efficient and knowledgeable service to the citizens of Jones County, and be a key resource for information about Jones County. \n \n\n \n \n\n About the Auditor\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Election Results\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Elections Website\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Employee Pay & Benefits Information\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Financial and Tax Information\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Historical Document Archive\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Passports\n \n \n\n \n \n\n Real Estate\n \n \n\n \n \n\n FAQ\n \n \n\n \nThe County Auditor's primary functions are: \n \n \n \nFinancial and Accounting Records: Prepares the County budget and monthly and annual financial reports of the County. Administers payroll and benefits for all county employees. Prepares claims and issues checks for payment of invoices, and maintains records of all county financial reports. \n \nReal Estate: Maintains official County property transfer and plat books. \n \nElections & Voter Registration: Conducts all elections for the county, cities, schools, special districts & the State of Iowa. Registers and maintains voter records. \n \nProperty Taxation: Prepares the annual report of assessed and taxable valuations of property in the county for use by all local governmental entities in the preparation of their budgets. Reviews and certifies budgets of all local governments in the county. Computes and certifies tax levies for taxing districts. Prepares tax lists for collection by the Treasurer. \n \nClerk to the Board of Supervisors: Prepares meeting agendas, prepares and maintains minutes of Board proceedings, and maintains Board records. \n \nCustodian of the Courthouse: Oversight of the care and maintenance of the courthouse, subject to the direction of the Board of Supervisors. \n \nMaintains files for Liquor & Cigarette Licenses as approved by the Board. \n \n \n\nAbout the Auditor \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \nPhone & Fax\n\n 319-462-2282 \n319-462-5815 (Fax)\n \nEmail\n\n auditor@jonescountyiowa.gov\n \nHours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\n\n Holiday Closures \nLocation\n\n Jones County Courthouse\n\n 500 W. Main St.\n\n Room 113\n Anamosa, IA 52205\n \n \n\n \n\n Whitney Hein\n \nCounty Auditor \nauditor@jonescountyiowa.gov \n319-462-2282 \n \n\n Kim Sorgenfrey\n \nDeputy \n \n\n Michele Lubben\n \nDeputy \n \n\n Vicki Starn\n \nDeputy \n \n\n Ashley Kurt\n \nDeputy \n \n\n Whitney Amos\n \nLand Use Administrator \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nJones County Courthouse\n\n 500 W. Main St\n\n Anamosa, IA 52205\n\n 319-462-5300\n\n Contact Us\n \n\n \nCourthouse Hours\n\n M - F 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\n\n Closed Holidays\n\n Department Hours May Vary\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n©2026 Jones County, Iowa · Title VI Nondiscrimination Notice · HIPAA Policies\n \npowered by \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVeterans Day (November 11, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving (November 26, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving - Friday After (November 27, 2026)\n \nChristmas Eve (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas (December 25, 2026)\n \nNew Year's Day (January 1, 2027)\n \n \n\n"
